From acb82791a1aa40b8529ef09f65e81156b1c05599 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Marcelo Poblete (via Claude)" <marcelopoblete.us@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 14 Sep 2026 00:25:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat: one map toolbar across every module, and matching
 satellite zoom
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Marcelo asked for the same map tools everywhere and for satellite to
zoom as deep in the module maps as it does in the general one.

- Conduit map: the basemap was one raster source whose tiles were
  swapped in place, so satellite inherited the street source's zoom
  ceiling and stopped short of where the general map can go. Now it is
  the same two sources toggled by visibility as ProjectMapCanvas, with
  the same per-source maxzoom (street 17, satellite 20), and the same
  Road / Sat / Hybrid options.
- Conduit and Fiber maps now use the general map's right-edge icon
  toolbar — layers panel, zoom in/out, and (Conduit) fit-to-elements —
  instead of each module having its own pill row.
- Conduit map also frames the duct bank on open rather than trusting
  the project-wide default centre, and calls resize() through a
  ResizeObserver so the canvas tracks its pane.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
